A||||5||batboy||feeling very humble||||1||
Z||000000||batboy||03-18-2000||06:56 AM||||I left a friend's place in Topeka last night and cruised down Gage Blvd. when a shiny, sleek, black Mercedes pulled up next to me. I look over and this baby is spotless and freshly waxed with a V12 emblem on the fender. A beautiful expensive looking blonde occupies the passenger seat. My faded black 85 Fiero GT sadly needs a bath. I rev up my crappy sounding engine with the leaking exhaust manifold. The blonde looks bored and yawns. The light turns green and I get a good start. I pull about a car length and hit second gear. The Mercedes gathers up speed and glides by me. No loud noise, just a soft whoosh and all I see are taillights. Oops! That'll teach me to mess with a car that costs more than my house did. Feeling very humble and very foolish, indeed. Hey, he had 6 more cylinders than my 2.8, what did I expect? Wait until I get the Batmobile back on the road again. Curse you black Mercedes!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gokart||03-18-2000||10:54 AM||||Hey, you had to try anyway! Credit you for that. Won't he be quite suprised thinking you'll be in the GT next time you pull up to him in the Batmobile! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000002||Spyder||03-18-2000||11:08 AM||||Well you probably won’t see that Mercedes again unless your not in the batmobile, that’s my luck.  <BR>I have done the same thing but in my old  Firebird, raced a 4 door Mercedes, he didn’t get me by much but it was enough to make me put my tail in-between my legs. ||||reg||1
